************** G E N E R A L   I N F O R M A T I O N *************5728 1451
                                                                  5728 1451
This evaluated data file is based on a software system built      5728 1451
around the nuclear model code TALYS [kon07], version 1.64. It is  5728 1451
part of a large collection of isotopic evaluations, all created by5728 1451
running the system with either adjusted or default input          5728 1451
parameters. This means that the data in the entire collection have5728 1451
been tested in detail for many isotopes against individual        5728 1451
experimental data, while for other isotopes it is only as good as 5728 1451
the global quality of TALYS at the moment. The mutual quality of  5728 1451
all individual data files is however consistent: The same set of  5728 1451
nuclear models is used and, equally important, the same ENDF-6    5728 1451
formatting procedures for each isotope. The data file has been    5728 1451
created automatically using the ENDF-6 format generator TEFAL.    5728 1451
                                                                  5728 1451
The resulting data file provides a complete representation of     5728 1451
nuclear data needed for transport, activation, damage, heating,   5728 1451
radioactivity, and shielding applications over the incident       5728 1451
neutron energy range from 1.e-11 to 200. MeV.                     5728 1451
                                                                  5728 1451
All transport and activation data for neutrons, charged particles,5728 1451
photons and residual nuclides are filed. This includes cross      5728 1451
sections, angular distributions, double-differential spectra,     5728 1451
isomeric production, discrete and continuum photon production     5728 1451
cross sections, residual production cross sections and recoils.   5728 1451
This general purpose evaluation can thus be used as both          5728 1451
transport and activation library.                                 5728 1451
                                                                  5728 1451
A complete set of covariance data is included, which is stored    5728 1451
in MF31-40.                                                       5728 1451
                                                                  5728 1451
**** N U C L I D E    S P E C I F I C   I N F O R M A T I O N ****5728 1451
                                                                  5728 1451
                      Resonance Range                             5728 1451
                                                                  5728 1451
  --------------------------------------------------------------- 5728 1451
  --------------------------------------------------------------- 5728 1451
                                                                  5728 1451
  General methodology: The global approach considered in this     5728 1451
          work is presented in the following paper: Modern        5728 1451
          nuclear data evaluation with the TALYS code system,     5728 1451
          A.J. Koning and D. Rochman, Nuclear Data Sheets 113     5728 1451
          (2012) 2841.                                            5728 1451
                                                                  5728 1451
  MF2:  Resolved resonance range  (RRR)                           5728 1451
       The RRR was generated with TARES-1.2, compiled on          5728 1451
       11-15-2014 08:01:51 PM at Petten, the, Netherlands. The RRR5728 1451
       expands from 0 to 3.561570E+4 eV, with resonance           5728 1451
       extracted from the "radiator" TARES database. A total of   5728 1451
       3 l-values are used and 294 resonances. The resonance      5728 1451
       formalism is multi-level Breit Wigner (MLBW).              5728 1451
       The ladder approach from the CALENDF code is used to       5728 1451
       generate statistical resonances in the unresolved          5728 1451
       resonance range. Therefore, the URR is translated into     5728 1451
       resolved resonance range. Explanations about the method    5728 1451
       can be found in the CALENDF manual: CEA-Report CEA-R-6277  5728 1451
       "CALENDF-2010: User manual" by J.C. Sublet, P. Ribon and   5728 1451
       M. Coste-Delcaux.                                          5728 1451
       The method of creating statistical resonances in the       5728 1451
       URR region is described in: "From average parameters to    5728 1451
       statistical resolved resonances", D. Rochman et al.,       5728 1451
       Annals of Nucl. Ene. 51 (2013) 60.                         5728 1451
       The s-wave average level spacing is 219.9 eV and           5728 1451
       the s-wave neutron strength is 0.0003261 1e-4.             5728 1451
                                                                  5728 1451
  MF32: Covariance file for resonance parameters                  5728 1451
        The compact format is used to represent the covariance    5728 1451
        information on the resonance parameters. Uncertainties    5728 1451
        come from compilations, EXFOR or existing libraries and   5728 1451
        correlations between parameters are obtained following    5728 1451
        the method presented in NIM/A 589 (2008) 85.              5728 1451
